# Kindle Oasis (8th generation), the "duet" board, stock firmware 5.16.2.1.1.
# Source-level only: this has never been built for a device, let alone run on
# one (docs/design/porting-to-other-models.md section 6). It exists so that the
# model-specific half of the configuration is written down where it was
# measured, instead of being carried as a note.

# 2G/2G user split (PAGE_OFFSET=0x80000000, VMSPLIT_2G in imx60_duet_defconfig),
# which is half the user address space and therefore fewer bits to randomise:
# Kconfig's own ceiling here is 8. Asking for 16 is what this board answers with
# 8, and taking the lower value is the honest reading of a hardware limit.
CONFIG_ARCH_MMAP_RND_BITS=8

# No ath6kl: imx60_duet_defconfig carries no ATH6KL_SDIO. The board is
# Broadcom -- board-mx6sl_wario.c introduces that code with "Broadcom 4343W
# Bluetooth structures" under CONFIG_MX6SL_WARIO_WOODY, which this defconfig
# sets -- so patch 0310's firmware policy, which is about the Atheros chip,
# stays off here.
# CONFIG_LAB126_ANDROID_ATH6KL_FIRMWARE is not set

# Wi-Fi is not a line in this file, and finding that out took building it
# (2026-10-23, docs/design/porting-to-other-models.md section 7). The short of
# it: the published archive has no Broadcom driver that compiles against the
# kernel it is published with.
#
# imx60_duet_defconfig names no Wi-Fi driver at all -- no ATH6KL, no BRCM,
# COMPAT_WIRELESS off -- so a kernel built from it has no Wi-Fi. The archive
# does carry brcm80211 twice, and neither copy is usable as it stands:
# drivers/staging/brcm80211 is an old snapshot that does not compile here
# (wl_iw.c reaches for dhd_wait_pend8021x and for iw_handler_def fields this
# kernel's wireless extensions no longer have), and
# compat-wireless/drivers/net/wireless/brcm80211 is newer but is wired into
# nothing: compat-wireless/Kconfig sources only ath, its Makefile builds only
# ath, and its own Makefile is missing the include line ath has. Worse, the
# two copies declare the same symbols (BRCMFMAC, BRCMUTIL), so they cannot be
# selected apart, and CONFIG_STAGING is on here because Android's binder and
# ashmem live there.
#
# So Oasis 1's Wi-Fi is a driver question, not a configuration one, and the
# answer this port already has for a driver it cannot build is the one to use:
# take the module off the device at install time. That needs a device, which
# is where this stops. (This used to say "the way the REAGL module is taken".
# It never was: the REAGL branch was removed unused on 2026-10-29.)

# This kernel is not the PW3's, and must not say it is: the module directory is
# named after this string, and a mismatch is how a module built for one model
# would be loaded on another.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-lab126-duet-android81"
